process.run` call with `text=True` also has an `encoding` keyword, covering all five call sites, with the expected count stated.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e","T9"],"criteria":["E1","E6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.5375,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["\"Add `encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\"` to every text-mode `subprocess.run` ... (the helpers at `:81`, `:136`, `:337` and the call at `:490`)\"","\"The `ssh-keygen -lf` call at `:228` ... also gets `encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\"` so the module has no locale-decoded call left.\"","No AC asserts on the call sites themselves; AC1 tests behavior only for paths whose output contains non-ASCII."],"finding":"The Approach commits to adding `encoding=\"utf-8\"` to five calls: the CLI helpers at :81, :136 and :337, the call at :490, and the `ssh-keygen` call at :228. It states that \"the module has no locale-decoded call left\". No acceptance criterion checks this. AC1 only proves the module's tests pass under a latin-1 locale. Calls whose output is ASCII, or whose assertions don't touch non-ASCII text, pass whether or not they get `encoding=`. A partial edit that fixes only `_verify_authorship` (:136) would therefore satisfy every AC.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f5527d0eb6bbbb542","impact":0.55,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach (five enumerated call sites) vs Acceptance Criteria","norm_id":"n783e16751b12b9ac","priority":0.4125,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["The executor patches only `_verify_authorship`. AC1, AC2 and AC3 all pass, but the helpers at :81 and :337 still decode with the locale codec and fail later when their output gains a non-ASCII character."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add an AC: \"Every `subprocess.run(..., text=True)` call in `tests/unit/test_identity_ts3_117b.py` also passes `encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\"`, checked by an AST walk of the module that finds 5 such calls and 0 without `encoding`.\" Alternatively, extend the existing `tests/unit/test_windows_text_encoding.py` guard to cover this test module.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.75,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"underspecified_certification","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add `tests/unit/test_identity_ts3_117b.py` to `_CLI_CONSUMERS` in `tests/unit/test_windows_text_encoding.py`, and list that file in Scope, so `make verify` checks this module's UTF-8 decoding on every PR.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.1875,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: \"the same pattern `tests/unit/test_windows_text_encoding.py` checks for product parents\"","tests/unit/test_windows_text_encoding.py:125-145 `_text_mode_runs_without_utf8` checks every text-mode `.run` with an AST walk; `_CLI_CONSUMERS` lists only src/ files","Plan Scope lists only `tests/unit/test_identity_ts3_117b.py`; the Testing section depends on a manual forced-locale run and a post-merge scheduled sweep","Plan: \"so the module has no locale-decoded call left\", which is the exact property the existing guard checks"],"finding":"The plan copies the repo's UTF-8 decode pattern but does not add this module to the guard that enforces it. `tests/unit/test_windows_text_encoding.py` already parametrizes `test_rebar_cli_output_is_decoded_as_utf8` over `_CLI_CONSUMERS` and fails on any text-mode `.run(...)` that lacks `encoding=\"utf-8\"`. Without that entry, nothing in the per-PR `make verify` stops a later edit, such as a new `verify-identity` helper, from bringing back a locale-decoded call. The forced-locale command is a manual step, and the Windows sweep is a scheduled run that only catches the problem after merge.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f006b2d28acc97d3d","impact":0.55,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach / Scope — tests/unit/test_windows_text_encoding.py `_CLI_CONSUMERS` (lines 116-122)","norm_id":"nf4abd4d2278da63b","priority":0.4125,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A later change adds another `subprocess.run([... 'rebar', ...], text=True)` to this module without `encoding`. Every PR check on Linux and macOS passes, and the next scheduled Windows sweep fails again with the same mojibake.","Someone refactors `_verify_authorship` and drops the `encoding` keyword. Nothing fails on the PR."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add `\"tests/unit/test_identity_ts3_117b.py\",` to the `_CLI_CONSUMERS` tuple in tests/unit/test_windows_text_encoding.py. Rename the tuple or update its docstring if it should now cover test parents as well as product parents. List that file under Scope, and add an acceptance criterion that `test_rebar_cli_output_is_decoded_as_utf8[tests/unit/test_identity_ts3_117b.py]` passes.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.75,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"yes","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"incomplete_enumeration","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Reword AC3 to require a manually dispatched `sweep (windows)` run on main after merge, completed, in which `test_off_keyring_signature_fails_enforcement` is reported as PASSED; record the run id and job id in a ticket comment.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e","T9"],"criteria":["E6","F1"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.325,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["\"does not list `test_off_keyring_signature_fails_enforcement` among its failures\"","Context cites a 'scheduled run' and a 'previous dispatch on main', which implies the workflow can be dispatched manually, but the plan never states that a dispatch is part of the work."],"finding":"AC3 is phrased negatively: the test must not be listed among the sweep's failures. That condition also holds if the Windows sweep never collects or runs the test, for example because of an earlier collection error, a skip, a cancelled job, or a filter. So the criterion can be met without the fix running on Windows. The AC also does not say whether the executor dispatches the sweep or waits for the next scheduled run, which affects whether it can be checked in-session.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fdd3870d7b14423d8","impact":0.55,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria — AC3 (`sweep (windows)` run on main after merge)","norm_id":"nd356723d95c8127f","priority":0.275,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["The Windows job errors before reaching tests/unit, or the module is skipped on Windows. The test is not 'among failures', so AC3 is ticked although the em-dash path never ran on cp1252.","The executor waits for a nightly scheduled run, so the ticket cannot close in the same session."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"AC3: \"After merge, dispatch the sweep workflow on main (`gh workflow run <sweep workflow> --ref main`). In job `sweep (windows)`, `tests/unit/test_identity_ts3_117b.py::test_off_keyring_signature_fails_enforcement` is reported PASSED, not absent or skipped. Record the run id and job id in a ticket comment.\"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"underspecified_certification","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}}],"impact_model_version":"plan-v5","material_fingerprint":"db04e926eb52d5f3","material_parts":{"children":["647ea2107ca5072f",0],"description":["9d05b577e067bba1",2458],"description_boxes":["0aad7da77d2ed59c",0],"file_impact":["0ea255a491db7f1e",1],"ticket_id":["e54a80fbeb7bba9e",19]},"metrics":{"cache_read_tokens":2